<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech CKD expects to make 1997 gross profit.</title>
<headline>Czech CKD expects to make 1997 gross profit.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech engineering group CKD Holding a.s. said on Tuesday that it expected a consolidated gross profit for 1997 of 597 million crowns after a 924.7 million crown net loss last year.</p>
<p>General Director Jiri Marousek added in a news conference that the company planned to stick to its original privatisation plan and pay its first dividend either on 1997 or 1998 earnings at the latest, but he did not forecast how much it would be.</p>
</text>
